# @see ADR-167
id: SLOP-003
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 4
action: advisory
title: AI hedge/caveat phrases
category: quality
severity: info
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .md .txt .rst .adoc
  exclude_paths: vendor/ node_modules/ SLOP-003
patterns:
  - regex: Note that this
    message: "AI hedge phrase — state the fact directly"
  - regex: Keep in mind that
    message: "AI hedge phrase — be direct"
  - regex: It's worth (noting|mentioning) that
    message: "AI hedge phrase — just say it"
  - regex: Please note that
    message: "AI hedge phrase — state facts directly"
  - regex: It should be noted that
    message: "AI passive hedge — be direct"
  - regex: As (mentioned|noted|discussed) (above|earlier|previously)
    message: "AI back-reference filler — use a link or remove"
  - regex: In (this|the following) (section|document|guide), we will
    message: "AI narration — the reader can see what follows"
  - regex: Let's (dive into|explore|take a look at|walk through)
    message: "AI conversational filler in documentation — be direct"
fix: Technical writing should be direct. State facts, don't narrate or hedge.
